# IB Gateway safety — SPX 0DTE is the protected party

One IB Gateway on the NY4 box (`spx-ny4`, FXVPS374628) is shared by **spx-0dte**,
**ls-algo**, and **this repo's portfolio hub**. spx-0dte runs a **live money**
options executor on it. Nothing here may cost it a connection, a client ID, a
market-data line, or a CPU core.

The full contract is in the repo-root `CLAUDE.md` and is mirrored in spx-0dte
`AGENTS.md` and ls-algo `CLAUDE.md`. A change to any clause must land in all
three in the same PR.

## The rule that governs everything else

**During market hours on a market day (09:30–16:00 ET, Mon–Fri, US market
holidays excluded), do not initiate anything that touches the Gateway.** Not a
connect, not a probe, not a "quick read-only check", not a service restart.
Diagnose from logs, the local ledger, D1, and the committed payload instead —
all of which are available without a socket.

If a task genuinely requires the Gateway during RTH, stop and ask the user
first, in chat, and say why it cannot wait until after 16:15 ET. Approval for
one such action is not approval for the next.

Off-hours work is fine, and after 16:15 ET on a weekday is the normal window.

## Never, under any circumstances

| Forbidden | Why |
|---|---|
| `reqGlobalCancel()` | Cancels every working order account-wide, including SPX's. **Test-enforced**: `test_ib_bridge.py` asserts no call site exists. |
| `reqAutoOpenOrders(True)` | Binds TWS-created orders to this client — how a hub session ends up owning an SPX order. **Test-enforced.** |
| Reusing another system's client ID | The hazard is grabbing an ID while its owner is mid-reconnect. Reserved: `{0, 17, 18, 19, 41, 77, 87, 90, 197, 207, 71, 72, 73, 82}` plus ls-algo worker ranges 241–273, 341–373, 551, 1041+. |
| Stopping/restarting the Gateway, or flipping its global Read-Only toggle | SPX rides through IBKR's daily restart by design. The **only** carve-out is spx-0dte's own `ibc_guard`. |
| Adding a streaming market-data subscription | Lines are one account-wide pool shared with SPX's option NBBO stream. The hub uses `snapshot=True` only and cancels in `finally`. Leak-tested. |
| Cancelling an order you cannot prove you own | Requires a `MAGIS|` orderRef **and** `clientId == 91`. |

## Client-ID map

| System | IDs |
