| spx-0dte | 17 (live executor), 18 (ibc_guard probe), 19 (market-data line probe, off-hours only), 87 (ES/SPX basis sampler) |
| ls-algo | 0, 41, 77, 90, 197/207, workers 241–273, 341–373, 551, 1041+ |
| this repo | 71/72/73 (sleeves), 81 (collector, read-only), 82 (observer, reserved), **91** (order bridge, sole transmitter) |
| Operator TWS | manual only |

New IDs go in this table, in `CLAUDE.md`, and in `CLIENT_ID_REGISTRY.md` **before
first use**. The Gateway accepts ~32 connections total; the hub holds at most 2.

## What is actually deployed (verified 2026-08-22)

Do not re-derive this from `deploy/README.md` — the README describes `/opt` +
system systemd, and the real install is **`/home/spx` under `spx`'s *user*
systemd**. `systemctl list-units` shows nothing; you must use:

```bash
sudo -u spx XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000 systemctl --user list-units --all 'portfolio-hub*'
```

| Thing | Location |
|---|---|
| Repo | `/home/spx/single-stock-investments` — a **file copy, no `.git`** |
| Ledger | `/home/spx/portfolio-hub/portfolio.db` |
| Venv | `/home/spx/portfolio-hub-venv` |
| Gateway API port | **7496** (the code default `IBKR_PORT=4002` is wrong for this host) |
| Reachability | UFW allows **OpenSSH only** → `ssh -N -L 7496:127.0.0.1:7496 spx-ny4` |
| Account / alias | id `U805366`; `IBKR_ACCOUNT_ALIAS=U805366` (same string, different concept) |

Because the repo there is a **copy**, code changes on `main` do not reach it.
A stale copy is how attribution silently broke: `allocation_policy.py` was
simply absent, so every position fell through to Michael's residual book.

## The Gateway is a session service

`ibc.service` starts, runs a few hours, and exits `0/SUCCESS` after the close.
Weekends it is down entirely. So `ConnectionRefusedError` on 127.0.0.1:7496 is
**normal off-hours, not a fault** — do not "fix" it by restarting anything, and
never by touching `ibc.service`.

## Background jobs must yield

Anything long-running deployed to NY4 runs `Nice>=15` + a `CPUQuota` +
`IOSchedulingClass=idle`, so the SPX executor never waits for a core. The box has
**4 cores**. Enforced via systemd drop-ins at
`~/.config/systemd/user/<unit>.service.d/10-spx-coexistence.conf`.

Retry loops need a real backoff. At the stock `RestartSec=5` the collector
produced **6,785 restarts and ~315k journal lines in a single day** against a
Gateway that was intentionally down.

## Read-only is a property of the connection, not an intention

The collector connects `readonly=True`, which is an **IB-API-level** bar on
transmitting, pins `clientId=81`, and makes no `reqMktData` call at all. Keep it
that way. "I'll just be careful" is not a safety; the flag is.
